  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nDry weather is expected through at least early Saturday as high \npressure moves east across the region. Rising 500 mb heights under \nshortwave ridging should result in high temperatures to slightly \nabove seasonable levels today. A digging shortwave trough is \nexpected to begin to advance out of the Midwest tonight into \nSaturday. Expect an increase in mid and high level clouds tonight \nthrough Saturday morning in advance of the trough.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nThe shortwave trough is expected to continue to deepen as it tracks \ntoward the Upper Ohio Valley region late Saturday and Sunday. At the \nsame time, an associated surface low is progged to track NE across \nthe Upper Ohio Valley/eastern Great Lakes region. Increasing \nmoisture and ascent with an initial lead shortwave should return \nshower and thunderstorm chances Saturday afternoon across Ohio, \noverspreading the remainder of the area Saturday night.\n\nPeriods of showers and scattered thunderstorms are expected on\nSunday as the main trough axis approaches, and the surface low\ntracks across the region. Clouds could limit instability, with\nML CAPE currently progged at 1000 J/kg or less, however, there\nis increased amount of vertical wind shear (up to 30kts). \nCurrent model runs are hinting at the chance for dry slots to\ndevelop in between periods of rain on Sunday. If these dry \nperiods are accompanied by some clearing, there would be an\nincrease in CAPE which combined with 30kts of vertical wind\nshear would improve the probability for severe weather to \ndevelop. \n\nLocally heavy rain will also be possible as PWATs approach 1.8 \ninches, though the potential dry slot Sunday afternoon ahead of\nthe surface low could limit this potential. The surface cold \nfront is currently expected to cross the area late Sunday/Sunday\nnight.\n\nModel ensembles then indicate a persistent trough across the\nEastern Great Lakes and Ohio Valley region early in the week.\nThis trough should weaken some through the week, though\nsignificant uncertainty exists in exact placement and strength.\nOverall, expect daily, diurnally driven shower and thunderstorm\nchances under this pattern.",
